鹜。在他愣神之时，胸前一凉，垂于胸前的发丝已被撩与耳后，凤傲天的双臂不知何时，已然滑过他的面颊两侧，修长的手指自他墨发间缠绕，不到片刻，便收起手臂，打量着他，“这云锦发带才适合你。”慕寒遥眸光微沉，心思一动，却不知他为何突然对他如此，但是，被一个男子竟如此亲昵地束发，而且，还是喜爱男色的摄政王，不免让他心生不自在，他微微向后，与凤傲天保持一定距离，垂眸，“草民多谢摄政王。”凤傲天对于他的疏离不以为意，满意地打量着自己的杰作，低头，将目光落在他腰间遮挡的黑布，随意抬手，便将黑布扯下，“如此晦气之物怎能沾染你的身体。”慕寒遥未料到凤傲天有如此的举动，先是为他亲自束带，如今，却说出如此只有男女之间才有的轻佻话语，让他着实有些沉闷，却不知如何回避。可是偏偏，这会如此之近的与凤傲天在一处，而且，连一丝遮蔽物都没有，他突然闪过一丝不该有的羞涩，更加不愿让他看到如今自己**的模样。如此一想，他心思更沉，他这是怎么了？连忙伸手，便要将那块黑布夺过来，却见凤傲天扯下之后，便轻轻一挥，那黑布乘着月色随风落下。他眸光冷厉，抬眸，正欲开口冷嗤，眼前一黑，一件长袍已然披在自己身上，他垂眸，却见那一双白皙的纤细手指熟练地将腰带系好，顺势打量了自己一番，低沉道，“本王再给你一次机会如何？”慕寒遥心下一冷，将内心的疑惑敛去，面色冷然，“草民……”他正要拒绝，却听到不远处传来的马蹄声，紧接着便看到玑柏带领着慕家军冲进了树林，进入了狼群的包围圈。慕寒遥面色一沉，暗叫不妙，抬眸，却看到凤傲天凤眸微眯，好整以暇地盯着他，“你可考虑清楚，不从本王者死，包括慕家军，本王的宝贝们可是饿了整整一日。”“将军，您在何处？末将等誓死跟随将军，同生共死！”玑柏并未见慕寒遥，却感觉到隐隐的不安，尤其是他身下的战马不停地摇晃，似是感觉到了危险将近。李肃驾马上前，行至玑柏身旁，“你看，这些残骸便是被狼群生吞活剥的栖国士兵。”玑柏低头，便看到他们马下皆是一片血肉模糊，他眉头一皱，“将军难道出事了？”“若是将军出事，那我等定要为将军报仇。”李肃眸光一沉道。“嗷呜……”又是一声凄厉的狼嚎声。适才隐去的狼群此刻正缓缓地前行，阴森的绿光透着嗜血的寒冷，逐渐逼近。战马亦是惊慌地嘶叫，不停地踢着马蹄，连连后退。慕寒遥看着如此情景，抬眸，再次看向凤傲天的时候，他紧握的双拳紧了又紧，最终还是松开，隐去漆黑瞳眸中深邃的幽光，“草民但凭摄政王处置。”－－－－－－题外话－－－－－－多谢亲耐哒孤离、映紫琉璃、夏夏、宝宝送滴评价票，么么哒！多谢亲耐哒映紫琉璃送的钻钻，么么哒！多谢亲耐哒墨蔓首、浅笑离歌、1297947598、13818131543、付海莲送滴花花，么么哒！", "source": "www.quanwenyuedu.io", "source_url": "https://www.quanwenyuedu.io/n/yetaicanbao/10.html", "_fixed": true, "content_en": "Volume 1 Regency 010 Feng Aotian, who would not obey this king, laughed loudly, \"Don't the Mu family's army always live and die together? You would rather die together than rush out to save him. Is this the so-called preferring to die together than to live?\" Ji Bai and others were startled, then suddenly realized, they quickly stopped drawing their swords and stood up together. Regardless of the fatigue of kneeling all day, they turned around and limped out of the camp. Feng Aotian raised her eyebrows lightly. She wanted to see how long Mu Hanyao could hold on. She walked out of the tent unhurriedly and raised her eyes. The moon was sparse and the stars were dim. The cold night was gloomy. Ji Bai had already issued an order and led the troops towards the woods five miles away. Si Xi followed Ye Jinsu closely, not daring to say anything. He raised his eyes slightly and looked at Feng Aotian's profile. Compared with the biting night wind, it was a bit colder. However, he felt that the regent today was different from the past, and he was a little more unpredictable and mysterious. The two souls threw Mu Hanyao directly into the woods and walked away. Mu Hanyao fell naked into the forest, against the moonlight, and put one hand on the ground. Just as he was about to get up, he felt the stickiness in his palm, and the strong and pungent smell of blood filled the forest, which could not be dissipated for a long time. He looked around vigilantly, surrounded by wreckage, covered in night, gusty winds, and the cold moonlight reflected in the dim woods, hitting the cold ground, revealing a chilling, bone-gnawing fear. He spread his palms that were pressed to the ground, and the stench of rotting flesh filled the air. His eyes were cold. Even though he was a general who was conquering the battlefield, he couldn't help but tremble when he saw such a tragic scene. He tried his best to cover up the nausea and anxiety in his heart. He stood up from the ground, and he was more convinced that the regent was indeed cruel. However, looking at the torn armor in front of me, soldiers of Qi Kingdom? The treasure Feng Aotian mentioned suddenly came to mind. He leaned over slightly, holding back his nausea, and then he was sure that they were bitten to death by wolves. Thinking of this, Mu Hanyao's mind became heavier. He picked up a long knife from the ground, found a piece of clean black cloth, covered the important parts, carefully observed the movements in the forest, and rushed out of the woods. \"Aww...\" A sad wolf howl broke through the sky and reached his ears. His dark eyes flashed with cold killing light. He pulled out the long knife, tapped his toes, and flew out. But it was too late. In an instant, he saw countless eerie green lights surrounding the entire forest, slowly approaching him. He was shocked, as he had never expected that there were wolves here. Wolves are the most ferocious animals. Any prey they target will not escape easily. Mu Hanyao is fully aware of his current situation and the danger is gradually approaching. Any movement he makes will lead to wolves attacking him. He had encountered wolves before, but not in such a huge pack. Now, he was alone, how could he face the attack of a pack of wolves? While he was thinking about a way to escape, he held his breath and quickly and lightly stood on a tall tree, observing the movement. Suddenly, a cold wind blew past him, and a figure stood beside him. He glanced sideways, but met a pair of phoenix eyes that seemed to be smiling but not smiling. The extraordinary handsome face and the dancing moonlight reflected Feng Aotian's look that was half playful and half cold. The corners of his mouth were slightly pursed, as if as soon as she opened her mouth, Mu Hanyao would be torn apart by wolves in the next second. Mu Hanyao was about to speak when he suddenly felt that the face in front of him was so close. The skin that could be broken by a blow was slightly cold, the red lips were as delicate as a woman's and raised a heart-warming smile. The eyebrows were as long as willows, and a pair of Feng's eyes are slightly curved, seemingly smiling, but he is also awe-inspiring, and his face is extremely gorgeous. If it weren't for his cruel temperament and love for men, his handsome face alone would attract many young talents from the Feng Kingdom. When he was stunned, his chest felt cold, and the hair hanging down on his chest had been pushed behind his ears. Feng Aotian's arms had slid across both sides of his cheeks without knowing when, and his slender fingers were entangled in his black hair. In less than a moment, he retracted his arms and looked at him, \"This cloud A brocade hair tie is suitable for you.\" Mu Hanyao's eyes darkened, and his thoughts moved, but he didn't know why he suddenly treated him like this. However, having his hair tied up so affectionately by a man, and who was also a regent who liked men, couldn't help but make him feel uncomfortable, and he leaned back slightly. , keeping a certain distance from Feng Aotian, lowered his eyes, \"Thank you, the common people, the regent.\" Feng Aotian didn't care about his alienation, and looked at his masterpiece with satisfaction. He lowered his head and focused his eyes on the black cloth covering his waist. He raised his hand casually and pulled off the black cloth. \"How could such an unlucky thing contaminate your body?\" Mu Hanyao did not expect that Feng Aotian would do such a thing. First, he tied the belt for him personally, but now, he said such frivolous words that could only be said between men and women, which made him feel a little depressed, but he didn't know how to avoid it. But unfortunately, being so close to Feng Aotian, and without even a trace of cover, he suddenly felt a trace of shyness that he shouldn't have, and he didn't want him to see his naked appearance. Thinking of this, he became even more worried. What happened to him? He quickly stretched out his hand to grab the piece of black cloth, but saw Feng Aotian pull it off, then wave it gently, and the black cloth fell with the wind in the moonlight. His eyes were cold and stern. He raised his eyes and was about to sneer. His eyes went dark. A robe was already draped on him. He lowered his eyes and saw a pair of white and slender fingers skillfully tying the belt. He looked at himself and said in a low voice, \"I will give you another chance.\" What will happen?\" Mu Hanyao felt cold, put away the doubts in his heart, and said with a cold expression, \"Caomin...\" He was about to refuse, but he heard the sound of horse hooves not far away, and then he saw Ji Bai leading the Mu family army into the woods and entered the circle of wolves. Mu Hanyao's face darkened, and he secretly screamed that something was wrong. He raised his eyes and saw Feng Aotian's eyes narrowed slightly, staring at him leisurely, \"You must think carefully. If you don't obey this king,", "title_en": "Chapter 10"}